Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 15:23:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/71] Reach GLM through Z.ai by restoring a chat-completions
 wire api

Upstream deleted `wire_api = "chat"`, which left no way to talk to an
OpenAI-compatible `/chat/completions` endpoint, and Z.ai serves the GLM
models over exactly that. The variant comes back, but not as a second code
path through the agent: the branch is confined to `codex-api`, where
`requests/chat.rs` rewrites the outgoing request and `sse/chat.rs` rewrites
the streamed frames back into the Responses shape. Everything above the
endpoint keeps seeing one wire protocol.

The `zai` provider is registered with its base url and `ZAI_API_KEY`, and
the client routes Chat providers through the SSE transport, since a
chat-completions endpoint has no WebSocket to negotiate.

Not yet exercised against the live endpoint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
